  "answer_text": "Great news! The latest iPhone lineup is widely available. Here's a full breakdown of where to buy and what's currently available:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcf1 Current iPhone Lineup\nApple's current flagship iPhone lineup includes the **iPhone 17e** (2026), **iPhone 17**, **iPhone 17 Pro**, **iPhone 17 Pro Max**, and **iPhone Air** (all 2025).\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\uded2 Where to Buy\n\n1. **Apple (apple.com or Apple Store)**\n   The best place to start. Apple offers two-hour delivery from an Apple Store, free delivery, or easy pickup options. You can also trade in your current iPhone or Android device and apply any credit toward your purchase.\n\n2. **Best Buy (bestbuy.com)**\n   Best Buy carries the latest Apple iPhones and accessories, including the newest iPhone models. You can look for trade-in discounts as well as offers made by coverage plans, and consider an unlocked iPhone for cellular plan flexibility or open-box products for discounted prices.\n\n3. **T-Mobile (t-mobile.com)**\n   T-Mobile carries the full current iPhone lineup, including the iPhone 17 Pro Max, iPhone 17 Pro, iPhone 17e, iPhone Air, and iPhone 17.\n\n4. **Other Carriers** such as AT&T and Verizon also typically carry the full iPhone lineup with plan-based deals and trade-in offers.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Quick Buying Tips\n\n- If budget is not a concern and you want the absolute best Apple makes, the **iPhone 17 Pro Max** is the top choice \u2014 it ships with the A19 Pro chip and a 6.9-inch ProMotion OLED display.\n- The **iPhone 17** offers many of the same features as the Pro models at a more affordable price and is recommended for most people \u2014 it's $300 less than the iPhone 17 Pro.\n- The **iPhone 17e** is Apple's most affordable option at **$599**, and comes with the A19 chip, 256GB base storage, MagSafe charging, and a 48MP camera.\n- The **iPhone Air** is Apple's boldest design in years \u2014 at just 5.5mm thin, it is the slimmest iPhone Apple has ever made.\n\nWould you like more details on any specific model or retailer?",
